From: openEuler RISC-V package maintenance
Subject: [PATCH] tests: discover the native RV64 compiler before cross compilers

QBE 1.3 check-rv64 probes only cross-prefixed compilers, even when the
test environment itself is riscv64. Reuse its existing native execution
path, keeping the explicit rv64 target and complete original test loop.
The native Linux branch already uses -lpthread for test drivers.

Applies-to: official QBE 1.3, archive SHA256
 d587905d620dc5e1d2bfa7c2cc642b9b837aa89a3188c6e37b53d756cf66e320
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (package-local compatibility fix)
Removal-condition: upstream check-rv64 discovers the native compiler.

--- a/tools/test.sh
+++ b/tools/test.sh
@@ -73,6 +73,10 @@ init() {
 		bin="$bin -t arm64"
 		;;
 	rv64)
+		if [ "$(uname -m)" = riscv64 ]; then
+			find_cc_and_qemu riscv64 "${CC:-cc}" "qemu-riscv64"
+			ccpost="-lpthread"
+		fi
 		for p in riscv64-linux-musl riscv64-linux-gnu
 		do
 			find_cc_and_qemu riscv64 "$p-gcc -no-pie -static" "qemu-riscv64"
